(6474320, 960889, 54645, '<td valign="top"><table align="center" width="95%"><tr><td><div class="textsm"><b>Originally posted by jagar:</b></div><hr/><i> This one stands out for me because of the subtle tones you used and that awesome reflection, a very nice candid. </i></td></tr></table> <br/> <br/>You also leveraged an aspect of Jagar''s street imagas that I love so much... and tendency to form two or three images in one frame. I''m referring to the textured wall gives the scene an imaginary context...very little structures like this in LA/OC.  Certainly the people have a lot to say...my favorite is the far left woman, peaking over her mug...I like to think she caught you.</td>', 'Originally posted by jagar: This one stands out for me because of the subtle tones you used and that awesome reflection, a very nice candid.   You also leveraged an aspect of Jagar''s street imagas that I love so much... and tendency to form two or three images in one frame. I''m referring to the textured wall gives the scene an imaginary context...very little structures like this in LA/OC.  Certainly the people have a lot to say...my favorite is the far left woman, peaking over her mug...I like to think she caught you.', '2011-07-18 13:03:27.000000', NULL, 0),
